.TH STRIP 1
.SH NAME
strip \- remove symbols and relocation bits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B strip
name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B strip
removes the symbol table and relocation bits ordinarily attached to
the output of the assembler and loader.
This is useful to save space after
a program has been debugged.
.PP
The effect of
.B strip
is the same as use of the
.B \-s
option of
.BR ld (1).
.SH FILES
.nf
.ta 1i
/tmp/stm?	temporary file
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ld(1)
.sp
